course: dictionary
lesson: 8807
title: Who is she?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «She» is a pronoun. It is a short word we use instead of a girl's or woman's name, so we do not have to repeat the name again and again. Before you can understand «she», you need to find who it points back to.
explain: «Ruby didn't start it, and the teacher never asked her. She thought she could always skip it.» The first «she» and the second «she» both mean Ruby. Read the sentences before it, find the girl who was named, and «she» belongs to her.
explain: «She» can also be used for a ship, a country or a car, as if it were a person: «The ship was old, but she still sailed well.» Context tells you which meaning you have.
fact: «She» is a pronoun. It stands in for a female person, such as a girl or woman, who has already been talked about.
fact: «Her» is the object or possessive form: «The teacher helped her» and «That bag is her bag».
fact: «She's» means she is or she has; «she'd» means she would or she had; «she'll» means she will.
fact: «She» can also mean a female animal: «Is your cat a he or a she?»
fact: In speech people say «Her and me went», but in writing say «She and I went».
exercise: «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room after Chloe's plaits are pulled so hard she cries.» Who does the second «she» mean? | *Chloe | The nurse | Lily | The plaits
exercise: «A girl in Toronto saw that her friend looked pale, and she told a teacher.» Who told a teacher? | *The girl in Toronto | The friend | Nobody | The teacher
exercise: Someone says «She'll be right, mate.» What does «she» mean here? | A girl named Mate | *Things in general, so everything will be fine | A ship that is sinking | A teacher
test: If Gran says «keep the change», telling her how much is left makes it an honest gift. Who does «her» mean? | *Gran | The change | The gift | The shopkeeper
test: Which is the right way to write it? | *She and I went to the park | Her and me went to the park | Her and I went to the park | Me and her went to the park
exam: «The ship left the harbour; she was loaded with apples.» What does «she» mean? | A girl | The harbour | *The ship | The apples
